$ bash seats/fleet-gate.selftest.sh

1. cold + ready — seats cold, work ready: loud nudge fires
  ok    cold+ready prints counts and the loud nudge

2. cold + empty — seats cold, no ready work: plain line, no nudge
  ok    cold+empty prints counts with no nudge

3. live — a seat is running, even with ready work: no nudge
  ok    live seat suppresses the nudge regardless of ready count

4. stale herald pid — every gate names the dead herald and last stderr
  ok    stale herald.pid is visible with the last stderr line

5. graceful degrade — bd absent: silent, exit 0
  ok    no bd on PATH: silent, exit 0

6. graceful degrade — adapter.ts absent: silent, exit 0
  ok    no adapter.ts: silent, exit 0

fleet-gate.sh works on this machine.
